---
description: Non-negotiables for the MyOS kernel — always in context
alwaysApply: true
---

Freestanding i386 kernel. No OS underneath, no libc, no runtime. Anything the
code calls, something in `kernel/` defines. Compiled with `-Werror`, so a
warning is a failed build.

Build and verify only through Docker — never install a toolchain on the host:

```
dev            build      (or: docker run --rm -v "$(pwd):/os" myos-dev make)
dev test       verify     boots headless, fails on any self-test failure
```

`make test` passing is the floor, not proof. Anything that draws has to be
looked at.

`kernel/font_atlas.c` and `kernel/wallpaper_image.c` are generated. Never edit
them by hand — regenerate with the scripts in `tools/`.

Deeper context is in @AGENTS.md and the files it points at. Read it before
changing bring-up order, the build, or anything in `kernel/`.
